{"sha":"cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","node_id":"C_kwDOA-MW79oAKGNhY2Y4ZTIzMGM4YjhlZDAyMWZlZWRkNTNmYTkyMDlhZWNiZTEzZDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"ivpr","email":"ivijayprasad@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-14T07:07:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-11-14T07:07:04Z"},"message":"Fix/tcp proxy close empty fin on downstream data (#49149)\n\nCommit Message: tcp_proxy: close downstream on empty FIN in\nON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA before upstream connect\n\nIn upstream_connect_mode ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA, a client that half-closes\n(FIN / end_stream)\nwithout sending any data never triggers the upstream connection, by\ndesign. Because half-close is\nenabled on the downstream connection, that FIN is not reported as\nRemoteClose, so nothing closed the\nsession. It stayed open until idle_timeout, or indefinitely if\nidle_timeout is unset.\n\nThis change closes the downstream connection in that case, with the\nlocal close reason\ntcp_proxy_downstream_closed_without_data. Other upstream connect modes\nare unchanged.\n\nAdditional Description:\n- Behaviour before: in ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA, an empty FIN before any data\nleft the downstream connection\n  open until idle_timeout.\n- Behaviour after: the same input closes the downstream connection\nimmediately (FlushWrite).\n- Scope: only when connect_mode is ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA, no data has been\nreceived yet\n(initial_data_received_ is false), and the buffer is empty with\nend_stream set. IMMEDIATE and\nON_DOWNSTREAM_TLS_HANDSHAKE are excluded, because they may have an\nupstream connect pending\n(or waiting on ODCDS / a retry timer), and their buffered end_stream\nmust still be flushed upstream.\n- A new LocalCloseReasons entry, TcpProxyDownstreamClosedWithoutData, is\nadded to\nenvoy/stream_info/stream_info.h. It appears as the connection\ntermination reason in access logs.\n\nAI assistance: parts of this change were drafted with generative AI\ntooling. The author has read\nand understands all code in this PR.\n\nRisk Level: Medium\nTesting:\n- Updated test/common/tcp_proxy/tcp_proxy_test.cc:\nEmptyDataWithEndStreamDoesNotTriggerConnection now\n  expects the downstream close with the new reason.\n- Added an assertion in ReceiveBeforeConnectDownstreamClosesWithoutData\nthat IMMEDIATE mode does not\nclose the downstream on an empty FIN while the upstream connect is in\nflight.\n- Unit tests: bazel test //test/common/tcp_proxy:tcp_proxy_test (run\nbefore merge; see note below).\n\nDocs Changes: N/A\nRelease Notes:\nchangelogs/current/bug_fixes/tcp_proxy__close-empty-fin-before-upstream.rst\nPlatform Specific Features: N/A\n[Optional Runtime guard:] None. (See note below.)\n[Optional Fixes #Issue]\n[Optional Fixes commit #PR or SHA]\n[Optional Deprecated:]\n[Optional API Considerations:]\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Prasad I V <prasad.iv@databricks.com>\nCo-authored-by: Prasad I V <prasad.iv@databricks.com>","tree":{"sha":"e818ea6a33ab7c0930cef44ab0f117f0bceb9eda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/git/trees/e818ea6a33ab7c0930cef44ab0f117f0bceb9eda"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/git/commits/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq+AiYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABRcQAHL/kKOYULXawtBG0v0AtnU4\nx53iwnHZ9hB1wFePZMMkVJa52KtrH63/tSJWIRGVJ2pb4wIgLID+tcDbR4RZ13i7\nJsZRw6iDpDykBgyVlpVCDvUTkYV0tEHaCL4zw2xXSmjVOv/dehguOcuJobxk1bEY\nB1lgwGWM2nan5azzC09dX7dd063Po8aCQTfL5ZSpdm+39f8HNoI84lfMCMV9Wpgt\ng0LPfqZpvzyiOIPsP/p+8FnXPOGG/xXXn2G05VI1saYAILS2p7GVYJYrNGma8Z2A\nqm+8SGvRkVLBHK2LMZAZLAUD06lW1p0fcmb1b6cpRMub0wEjHdqMDLFeLOBq9wdU\nfzy0xry/YJLIekkPS4PkWgWFilmDy8lw89daiAdMLXRD4aBV7e4zHcX8dwwWOZm1\nAIDZDIbIRIUXJf0BwzDdiLZKfxoM4B90Pkc5uxgD/BqAcHqk/owWaIvbBJFxm80R\n9uEFPd3cqOxikREVy0bhdYUq3oYN9SDQdWkied4mItY+TgOF3p73ZxT3ax1WHtjm\nxi1+xFFDg6zMR9UD2NGbK6qEpwjZVZS2RCzlHMdoXLfNPvP4URd6Un1G1RweYNVb\nHNe+k2R0Ip7g962zX+ZU7aTJLl9j/HohW5FmXpmi/Tw40mfWn6/ep8az/L2+eetY\n1EC6XwD9lQ/tCzK5oF3m\n=eHQk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e818ea6a33ab7c0930cef44ab0f117f0bceb9eda\nparent 6cff6c276810150bdbb0ffdb831385c06b22ec5a\nauthor ivpr <ivijayprasad@gmail.com> 1794640024 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1794640024 -0800\n\nFix/tcp proxy close empty fin on downstream data (#49149)\n\nCommit Message: tcp_proxy: close downstream on empty FIN in\nON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA before upstream connect\n\nIn upstream_connect_mode ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA, a client that half-closes\n(FIN / end_stream)\nwithout sending any data never triggers the upstream connection, by\ndesign. Because half-close is\nenabled on the downstream connection, that FIN is not reported as\nRemoteClose, so nothing closed the\nsession. It stayed open until idle_timeout, or indefinitely if\nidle_timeout is unset.\n\nThis change closes the downstream connection in that case, with the\nlocal close reason\ntcp_proxy_downstream_closed_without_data. Other upstream connect modes\nare unchanged.\n\nAdditional Description:\n- Behaviour before: in ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA, an empty FIN before any data\nleft the downstream connection\n  open until idle_timeout.\n- Behaviour after: the same input closes the downstream connection\nimmediately (FlushWrite).\n- Scope: only when connect_mode is ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA, no data has been\nreceived yet\n(initial_data_received_ is false), and the buffer is empty with\nend_stream set. IMMEDIATE and\nON_DOWNSTREAM_TLS_HANDSHAKE are excluded, because they may have an\nupstream connect pending\n(or waiting on ODCDS / a retry timer), and their buffered end_stream\nmust still be flushed upstream.\n- A new LocalCloseReasons entry, TcpProxyDownstreamClosedWithoutData, is\nadded to\nenvoy/stream_info/stream_info.h. It appears as the connection\ntermination reason in access logs.\n\nAI assistance: parts of this change were drafted with generative AI\ntooling. The author has read\nand understands all code in this PR.\n\nRisk Level: Medium\nTesting:\n- Updated test/common/tcp_proxy/tcp_proxy_test.cc:\nEmptyDataWithEndStreamDoesNotTriggerConnection now\n  expects the downstream close with the new reason.\n- Added an assertion in ReceiveBeforeConnectDownstreamClosesWithoutData\nthat IMMEDIATE mode does not\nclose the downstream on an empty FIN while the upstream connect is in\nflight.\n- Unit tests: bazel test //test/common/tcp_proxy:tcp_proxy_test (run\nbefore merge; see note below).\n\nDocs Changes: N/A\nRelease Notes:\nchangelogs/current/bug_fixes/tcp_proxy__close-empty-fin-before-upstream.rst\nPlatform Specific Features: N/A\n[Optional Runtime guard:] None. (See note below.)\n[Optional Fixes #Issue]\n[Optional Fixes commit #PR or SHA]\n[Optional Deprecated:]\n[Optional API Considerations:]\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Prasad I V <prasad.iv@databricks.com>\nCo-authored-by: Prasad I V <prasad.iv@databricks.com>","verified_at":"2026-11-14T07:07:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/commits/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","html_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/commit/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/commits/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/comments","author":{"login":"ivpr","id":14174960,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTc0OTYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14174960?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivpr","html_url":"https://github.com/ivpr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivpr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivpr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivpr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivpr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivpr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivpr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivpr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivpr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivpr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6cff6c276810150bdbb0ffdb831385c06b22ec5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/commits/6cff6c276810150bdbb0ffdb831385c06b22ec5a","html_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/commit/6cff6c276810150bdbb0ffdb831385c06b22ec5a"}],"stats":{"total":191,"additions":186,"deletions":5},"files":[{"sha":"25470fbf12195b56b4578579ceb3c5ec594cd279","filename":"changelogs/current/bug_fixes/tcp_proxy__close-empty-fin-before-upstream.rst","status":"added","additions":6,"deletions":0,"changes":6,"blob_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/changelogs%2Fcurrent%2Fbug_fixes%2Ftcp_proxy__close-empty-fin-before-upstream.rst","raw_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/raw/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/changelogs%2Fcurrent%2Fbug_fixes%2Ftcp_proxy__close-empty-fin-before-upstream.rst","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/contents/changelogs%2Fcurrent%2Fbug_fixes%2Ftcp_proxy__close-empty-fin-before-upstream.rst?ref=cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+Fixed :ref:`tcp_proxy <config_network_filters_tcp_proxy>` in ``upstream_connect_mode: ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA``\n+leaving a downstream connection open until ``idle_timeout`` when the client half-closed without\n+sending any data. Envoy now closes such a connection at once and records\n+``tcp_proxy_downstream_closed_without_data`` as its downstream local close reason, shown by\n+``%DOWNSTREAM_LOCAL_CLOSE_REASON%``, and counts it in ``downstream_cx_closed_without_data``. These\n+connections no longer reach ``idle_timeout``. Other connect modes are unchanged."},{"sha":"60ae0859444689eadd67ad37e1ba72b68845d4eb","filename":"docs/root/configuration/listeners/network_filters/tcp_proxy_filter.rst","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0,"changes":3,"blob_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/docs%2Froot%2Fconfiguration%2Flisteners%2Fnetwork_filters%2Ftcp_proxy_filter.rst","raw_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/raw/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/docs%2Froot%2Fconfiguration%2Flisteners%2Fnetwork_filters%2Ftcp_proxy_filter.rst","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/contents/docs%2Froot%2Fconfiguration%2Flisteners%2Fnetwork_filters%2Ftcp_proxy_filter.rst?ref=cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","patch":"@@ -69,6 +69,8 @@ and how early data is buffered.\n * ``ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA``: Wait for initial data from the downstream connection before establishing the upstream\n   connection. This allows preceding filters to inspect the initial data before the upstream connection is established.\n   This mode **requires** ``max_early_data_bytes`` to be set.\n+  If the downstream half-closes without sending any data, the connection is closed immediately, without connecting upstream.\n+  The close reason is ``tcp_proxy_downstream_closed_without_data``, and the connection is counted in ``downstream_cx_closed_without_data``.\n * ``ON_DOWNSTREAM_TLS_HANDSHAKE``: Wait for the downstream TLS handshake to complete before establishing the upstream\n   connection. This allows access to the full TLS connection information, including client certificates and negotiated\n   parameters. This mode is only effective when the downstream connection uses TLS. For non-TLS connections, it behaves\n@@ -228,6 +230,7 @@ The downstream statistics are rooted at *tcp.<stat_prefix>.* with the following\n   downstream_cx_total, Counter, Total number of connections handled by the filter\n   downstream_cx_no_route, Counter, Number of connections for which no matching route was found or the cluster for the route was not found\n   downstream_cx_drain_close, Counter, Total number of connections closed due to drain close\n+  downstream_cx_closed_without_data, Counter, \"Total number of connections closed because the downstream half-closed without sending any data in ``ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA`` mode before any upstream connection was attempted\"\n   downstream_cx_overload_close, Counter, Total number of connections closed due to overload manager load shedding\n   downstream_cx_tx_bytes_total, Counter, Total bytes written to the downstream connection\n   downstream_cx_tx_bytes_buffered, Gauge, Total bytes currently buffered to the downstream connection"},{"sha":"ac61b456b1693ab8c992a7810cf4ca5b26f62072","filename":"envoy/stream_info/stream_info.h","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":0,"changes":4,"blob_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/envoy%2Fstream_info%2Fstream_info.h","raw_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/raw/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/envoy%2Fstream_info%2Fstream_info.h","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/contents/envoy%2Fstream_info%2Fstream_info.h?ref=cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","patch":"@@ -287,6 +287,10 @@ struct LocalCloseReasonValues {\n   const std::string TriggeredDelayedCloseTimeout = \"triggered_delayed_close_timeout\";\n   const std::string TcpProxyInitializationFailure = \"tcp_initializion_failure:\";\n   const std::string TcpProxyDrainClose = \"tcp_proxy_drain_close\";\n+  // Downstream half-closed with no data while tcp_proxy had not yet established (and will not\n+  // establish) an upstream connection, e.g. ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA with an empty FIN.\n+  const std::string TcpProxyDownstreamClosedWithoutData =\n+      \"tcp_proxy_downstream_closed_without_data\";\n   const std::string TcpSessionIdleTimeout = \"tcp_session_idle_timeout\";\n   const std::string MaxConnectionDurationReached = \"max_connection_duration_reached\";\n   const std::string ClosingUpstreamTcpDueToDownstreamRemoteClose ="},{"sha":"a02a7b9751a1f4b72448b687a674827521f59766","filename":"source/common/tcp_proxy/tcp_proxy.cc","status":"modified","additions":17,"deletions":0,"changes":17,"blob_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/source%2Fcommon%2Ftcp_proxy%2Ftcp_proxy.cc","raw_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/raw/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/source%2Fcommon%2Ftcp_proxy%2Ftcp_proxy.cc","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/contents/source%2Fcommon%2Ftcp_proxy%2Ftcp_proxy.cc?ref=cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","patch":"@@ -1163,6 +1163,23 @@ Network::FilterStatus Filter::onData(Buffer::Instance& data, bool end_stream) {\n           return Network::FilterStatus::StopIteration;\n         }\n       }\n+    } else if (connect_mode_ == UpstreamConnectMode::ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA &&\n+               !initial_data_received_ && end_stream && early_data_buffer_.length() == 0) {\n+      // ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA never connects upstream for a downstream that half-closes before\n+      // sending data. Half-close is enabled, so that FIN is not a RemoteClose, and the session\n+      // would otherwise stay open until idle_timeout or max_downstream_connection_duration ends\n+      // it, or indefinitely when idle_timeout is 0s and no duration is set.\n+      //\n+      // Other modes have already started or scheduled an upstream connect, and they flush the\n+      // buffered end_stream to it once it connects.\n+      ENVOY_CONN_LOG(debug,\n+                     \"Downstream closed without data before upstream connect; closing connection\",\n+                     read_callbacks_->connection());\n+      config_->stats().downstream_cx_closed_without_data_.inc();\n+      read_callbacks_->connection().close(\n+          Network::ConnectionCloseType::FlushWrite,\n+          StreamInfo::LocalCloseReasons::get().TcpProxyDownstreamClosedWithoutData);\n+      return Network::FilterStatus::StopIteration;\n     }\n \n     // Read-disable downstream when receiving early data to prevent excessive buffering."},{"sha":"475da5588e6f35b66ee470697eb54aa7b7435705","filename":"source/common/tcp_proxy/tcp_proxy.h","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changes":1,"blob_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/source%2Fcommon%2Ftcp_proxy%2Ftcp_proxy.h","raw_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/raw/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/source%2Fcommon%2Ftcp_proxy%2Ftcp_proxy.h","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/contents/source%2Fcommon%2Ftcp_proxy%2Ftcp_proxy.h?ref=cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","patch":"@@ -62,6 +62,7 @@ constexpr absl::string_view ReceiveBeforeConnectKey = \"envoy.tcp_proxy.receive_b\n  */\n #define ALL_TCP_PROXY_STATS(COUNTER, GAUGE)                                                        \\\n   COUNTER(downstream_cx_drain_close)                                                               \\\n+  COUNTER(downstream_cx_closed_without_data)                                                       \\\n   COUNTER(downstream_cx_no_route)                                                                  \\\n   COUNTER(downstream_cx_overload_close)                                                            \\\n   COUNTER(downstream_cx_rx_bytes_total)                                                            \\"},{"sha":"45dc6932bd250ef4dee2da9e002cf876580b7eca","filename":"test/common/tcp_proxy/tcp_proxy_test.cc","status":"modified","additions":112,"deletions":5,"changes":117,"blob_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/test%2Fcommon%2Ftcp_proxy%2Ftcp_proxy_test.cc","raw_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/raw/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/test%2Fcommon%2Ftcp_proxy%2Ftcp_proxy_test.cc","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/contents/test%2Fcommon%2Ftcp_proxy%2Ftcp_proxy_test.cc?ref=cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","patch":"@@ -1045,9 +1045,11 @@ TEST_P(TcpProxyTest, ReceiveBeforeConnectEarlyDataWithEndStream) {\n TEST_P(TcpProxyTest, ReceiveBeforeConnectDownstreamClosesWithoutData) {\n   setup(/*connections=*/1, /*set_redirect_records=*/false, /*receive_before_connect=*/true);\n \n-  // Downstream closes without sending any data.\n+  // Downstream closes without sending any data. The upstream connect is already in flight\n+  // (IMMEDIATE), so the downstream must not be closed here; the FIN is buffered for the upstream.\n   Buffer::OwnedImpl empty_buffer;\n   EXPECT_CALL(*upstream_connections_.at(0), write(_, _)).Times(0);\n+  EXPECT_CALL(filter_callbacks_.connection_, close(_, _)).Times(0);\n   filter_->onData(empty_buffer, /*end_stream=*/true);\n \n   // When upstream connection is established, the end_stream signal should be sent even though\n@@ -2485,6 +2487,82 @@ TEST_P(TcpProxyTest, OdcdsClusterMissingCauseConnectionClose) {\n   ASSERT_FALSE(upstream_connection_establishment_latency.has_value());\n }\n \n+// An empty FIN that arrives while an on demand cluster lookup is pending in IMMEDIATE mode must not\n+// close the downstream. It is buffered as end_stream and flushed upstream once the connection is\n+// established. The close is limited to ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA, which is the only mode that never\n+// connects upstream on its own.\n+TEST_P(TcpProxyTest, ImmediateEmptyFinWhileOnDemandClusterPendingIsFlushedUpstream) {\n+  auto config = onDemandConfig();\n+  config.mutable_max_early_data_bytes()->set_value(1024);\n+  mock_odcds_api_handle_ = Upstream::MockOdCdsApiHandle::create().release();\n+\n+  // The first lookup finds no cluster and triggers on demand discovery. The second lookup, after\n+  // discovery completes, finds the cluster.\n+  EXPECT_CALL(factory_context_.server_factory_context_.cluster_manager_,\n+              getThreadLocalCluster(\"fake_cluster\"))\n+      .WillOnce(Return(nullptr))\n+      .WillOnce(\n+          Return(&factory_context_.server_factory_context_.cluster_manager_.thread_local_cluster_))\n+      .RetiresOnSaturation();\n+\n+  Upstream::ClusterDiscoveryCallbackPtr cluster_discovery_callback;\n+  EXPECT_CALL(*mock_odcds_api_handle_, requestOnDemandClusterDiscovery(\"fake_cluster\", _, _))\n+      .WillOnce([&](auto&&, auto&& cb, auto&&) {\n+        cluster_discovery_callback = std::move(cb);\n+        return std::make_unique<Upstream::MockClusterDiscoveryCallbackHandle>();\n+      });\n+\n+  // Use connections=0 so setup() does not call onNewConnection(). With ODCDS missing the cluster,\n+  // onNewConnection returns StopIteration even though max_early_data_bytes enables\n+  // receive_before_connect, so setup(1, ...) cannot reconcile those expectations.\n+  setup(0, /*set_redirect_records=*/false, /*receive_before_connect=*/true, config);\n+\n+  upstream_connections_.push_back(std::make_unique<NiceMock<Network::MockClientConnection>>());\n+  upstream_connection_data_.push_back(\n+      std::make_unique<NiceMock<Tcp::ConnectionPool::MockConnectionData>>());\n+  ON_CALL(*upstream_connection_data_.back(), connection())\n+      .WillByDefault(ReturnRef(*upstream_connections_.back()));\n+  upstream_hosts_.push_back(std::make_shared<NiceMock<Upstream::MockHost>>());\n+  conn_pool_handles_.push_back(\n+      std::make_unique<NiceMock<Envoy::ConnectionPool::MockCancellable>>());\n+  ON_CALL(*upstream_hosts_.at(0), address())\n+      .WillByDefault(Return(*Network::Utility::resolveUrl(\"tcp://127.0.0.1:80\")));\n+  EXPECT_CALL(*upstream_connections_.at(0), dispatcher())\n+      .WillRepeatedly(ReturnRef(filter_callbacks_.connection_.dispatcher_));\n+\n+  {\n+    testing::InSequence sequence;\n+    EXPECT_CALL(factory_context_.server_factory_context_.cluster_manager_.thread_local_cluster_,\n+                tcpConnPool(_, _, _))\n+        .WillOnce(Return(Upstream::TcpPoolData([]() {}, &conn_pool_)))\n+        .RetiresOnSaturation();\n+    EXPECT_CALL(conn_pool_, newConnection(_))\n+        .WillOnce(\n+            [=, this](Tcp::ConnectionPool::Callbacks& cb) -> Tcp::ConnectionPool::Cancellable* {\n+              conn_pool_callbacks_.push_back(&cb);\n+              return onNewConnection(conn_pool_handles_.at(0).get());\n+            })\n+        .RetiresOnSaturation();\n+    EXPECT_CALL(factory_context_.server_factory_context_.cluster_manager_.thread_local_cluster_,\n+                tcpConnPool(_, _, _))\n+        .WillRepeatedly(Return(std::nullopt));\n+  }\n+\n+  // ODCDS is pending, so onNewConnection stops iteration even with receive_before_connect.\n+  EXPECT_EQ(Network::FilterStatus::StopIteration, filter_->onNewConnection());\n+\n+  // The downstream half-closes while the lookup is still pending. Nothing may close it.\n+  EXPECT_CALL(filter_callbacks_.connection_, close(_, _)).Times(0);\n+  Buffer::OwnedImpl empty_data;\n+  EXPECT_EQ(Network::FilterStatus::StopIteration, filter_->onData(empty_data, true));\n+\n+  // Discovery completes. The buffered end_stream must reach the upstream on connect.\n+  std::invoke(*cluster_discovery_callback, Upstream::ClusterDiscoveryStatus::Available);\n+  EXPECT_CALL(*upstream_connections_.at(0), write(BufferString(\"\"), /*end_stream*/ true));\n+  // Empty FIN with max_early_data_bytes > 0 does not read-disable the downstream.\n+  raiseEventUpstreamConnected(0, /*expect_read_enable=*/false);\n+}\n+\n // Test that upstream transport failure message is reflected in access logs.\n TEST_P(TcpProxyTest, UpstreamConnectFailureStreamInfoAccessLog) {\n   setup(1, accessLogConfig(\"%UPSTREAM_TRANSPORT_FAILURE_REASON%\"));\n@@ -2871,7 +2949,8 @@ TEST_P(TcpProxyTest, SingleConnectionTriggerWithMultipleDataChunks) {\n   EXPECT_EQ(connection_attempts, 1);\n }\n \n-// Test empty data with end_stream doesn't trigger connection in ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA mode.\n+// Test empty data with end_stream doesn't trigger connection in ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA mode, and\n+// closes the downstream connection instead of leaving it open until idle_timeout.\n TEST_P(TcpProxyTest, EmptyDataWithEndStreamDoesNotTriggerConnection) {\n   envoy::extensions::filters::network::tcp_proxy::v3::TcpProxy config = defaultConfig();\n   config.set_upstream_connect_mode(\n@@ -2884,12 +2963,40 @@ TEST_P(TcpProxyTest, EmptyDataWithEndStreamDoesNotTriggerConnection) {\n \n   EXPECT_EQ(Network::FilterStatus::Continue, filter_->onNewConnection());\n \n-  // Empty data with end_stream should NOT trigger connection.\n+  // An empty FIN must not create an upstream connection or read-disable the downstream. It must\n+  // close the downstream with the dedicated local close reason.\n+  EXPECT_CALL(factory_context_.server_factory_context_.cluster_manager_.thread_local_cluster_,\n+              tcpConnPool(_, _, _))\n+      .Times(0);\n+  EXPECT_CALL(filter_callbacks_.connection_, readDisable(_)).Times(0);\n+  EXPECT_CALL(filter_callbacks_.connection_,\n+              close(Network::ConnectionCloseType::FlushWrite,\n+                    StreamInfo::LocalCloseReasons::get().TcpProxyDownstreamClosedWithoutData));\n   Buffer::OwnedImpl empty_data;\n   EXPECT_EQ(Network::FilterStatus::StopIteration, filter_->onData(empty_data, true));\n+}\n+\n+// Same as above with max_early_data_bytes set to 0. The downstream is read-disabled on every\n+// early-data read in this configuration, so the close must happen before that point.\n+TEST_P(TcpProxyTest, EmptyDataWithEndStreamZeroEarlyDataBytesDoesNotReadDisable) {\n+  envoy::extensions::filters::network::tcp_proxy::v3::TcpProxy config = defaultConfig();\n+  config.set_upstream_connect_mode(\n+      envoy::extensions::filters::network::tcp_proxy::v3::ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA);\n+  config.mutable_max_early_data_bytes()->set_value(0);\n+\n+  setupOnDownstreamDataMode(config, true);\n+\n+  EXPECT_EQ(Network::FilterStatus::Continue, filter_->onNewConnection());\n \n-  // No connection should be established.\n-  EXPECT_TRUE(conn_pool_callbacks_.empty());\n+  EXPECT_CALL(factory_context_.server_factory_context_.cluster_manager_.thread_local_cluster_,\n+              tcpConnPool(_, _, _))\n+      .Times(0);\n+  EXPECT_CALL(filter_callbacks_.connection_, readDisable(_)).Times(0);\n+  EXPECT_CALL(filter_callbacks_.connection_,\n+              close(Network::ConnectionCloseType::FlushWrite,\n+                    StreamInfo::LocalCloseReasons::get().TcpProxyDownstreamClosedWithoutData));\n+  Buffer::OwnedImpl empty_data;\n+  EXPECT_EQ(Network::FilterStatus::StopIteration, filter_->onData(empty_data, true));\n }\n \n // Test load shedding in onData() when receive_before_connect is enabled."},{"sha":"e4135712c09241c5870ecccad8cb6bf4159d7f37","filename":"test/integration/tcp_proxy_integration_test.cc","status":"modified","additions":43,"deletions":0,"changes":43,"blob_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/test%2Fintegration%2Ftcp_proxy_integration_test.cc","raw_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/raw/cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8/test%2Fintegration%2Ftcp_proxy_integration_test.cc","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/contents/test%2Fintegration%2Ftcp_proxy_integration_test.cc?ref=cacf8e230c8b8ed021feedd53fa9209aecbe13d8","patch":"@@ -2974,6 +2974,49 @@ TEST_P(TcpProxyIntegrationTest, NoDataDoesNotTriggerConnection) {\n   tcp_client->close();\n }\n \n+// Verifies that a client which half-closes without sending any data is closed at once in\n+// ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA mode, without an upstream connection, and that the close reason is logged.\n+TEST_P(TcpProxyIntegrationTest, OnDownstreamDataEmptyFinClosesWithoutUpstream) {\n+  std::string access_log_path = TestEnvironment::temporaryPath(\n+      fmt::format(\"access_log{}{}.txt\", version_ == Network::Address::IpVersion::v4 ? \"v4\" : \"v6\",\n+                  TestUtility::uniqueFilename()));\n+  config_helper_.addConfigModifier([&](envoy::config::bootstrap::v3::Bootstrap& bootstrap) -> void {\n+    auto* listener = bootstrap.mutable_static_resources()->mutable_listeners(0);\n+    auto* filter_chain = listener->mutable_filter_chains(0);\n+    auto* config_blob = filter_chain->mutable_filters(0)->mutable_typed_config();\n+    ASSERT_TRUE(config_blob->Is<envoy::extensions::filters::network::tcp_proxy::v3::TcpProxy>());\n+    auto tcp_proxy_config =\n+        MessageUtil::anyConvert<envoy::extensions::filters::network::tcp_proxy::v3::TcpProxy>(\n+            *config_blob);\n+    tcp_proxy_config.set_upstream_connect_mode(\n+        envoy::extensions::filters::network::tcp_proxy::v3::ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA);\n+    tcp_proxy_config.mutable_max_early_data_bytes()->set_value(8192);\n+    auto* access_log = tcp_proxy_config.add_access_log();\n+    access_log->set_name(\"accesslog\");\n+    envoy::extensions::access_loggers::file::v3::FileAccessLog access_log_config;\n+    access_log_config.set_path(access_log_path);\n+    access_log_config.mutable_log_format()->mutable_text_format_source()->set_inline_string(\n+        \"%DOWNSTREAM_LOCAL_CLOSE_REASON%\");\n+    std::ignore = access_log->mutable_typed_config()->PackFrom(access_log_config);\n+    std::ignore = config_blob->PackFrom(tcp_proxy_config);\n+  });\n+  initialize();\n+\n+  IntegrationTcpClientPtr tcp_client = makeTcpConnection(lookupPort(\"tcp_proxy\"));\n+  // Half-close the downstream without sending any data.\n+  ASSERT_TRUE(tcp_client->write(\"\", /*end_stream=*/true));\n+  // Envoy closes the downstream connection instead of leaving it open until idle_timeout.\n+  tcp_client->waitForDisconnect();\n+\n+  // No upstream connection is made for a connection that never sent data.\n+  FakeRawConnectionPtr fake_upstream_connection;\n+  ASSERT_FALSE(fake_upstreams_[0]->waitForRawConnection(fake_upstream_connection,\n+                                                        std::chrono::milliseconds(1000)));\n+\n+  EXPECT_EQ(waitForAccessLog(access_log_path), \"tcp_proxy_downstream_closed_without_data\");\n+  test_server_->waitForCounter(\"tcp.tcpproxy_stats.downstream_cx_closed_without_data\", Eq(1));\n+}\n+\n // Test edge case where max_buffered_bytes=0 with ON_DOWNSTREAM_DATA mode.\n TEST_P(TcpProxyIntegrationTest, ZeroBufferWithOnDownstreamData) {\n   config_helper_.addConfigModifier([](envoy::config::bootstrap::v3::Bootstrap& bootstrap) {"}]}